@ 46.13 - Old Norse to Faroese Vowel Shift
# citation: johanpeturdam NB: “The reflexes of the vowels are given in the order of their reflex when stressed/long, and unstressed/short”
	{a,æ:[+long]} > ɛa / a
	a:[+long] > ɔa “(except NE of the Faroes / ɔ
	ɔa “(except NE of the Faroes > a:[+long])” / ɔ
	e > e:[+long] / ɛ
	e:[+long] > ɛa “(except Suðuroy / a “(except Suðuroy → ɛ)”
	ɛa “(except Suðuroy > e:[+long])” / a “(except Suðuroy → ɛ)”
	{i,y} > i:[+long] / ɪ
	{i:[+long],y:[+long]} > ʊi / ʊ(i)
	o > o:[+long] / ɔ
	o:[+long] > {ɔu,ɛu,œu} / œ “(except Suðuroy → ɔ)”
	u > u:[+long] / short: ʊ / unstressed: {o,ɔ}
	u:[+long] > ʉu / ʏ
	{œ,ɔ} > ø:[+long]/œ “(except Suðuroy
	ø:[+long]/œ “(except Suðuroy > ʏ)”